# Internal documentation — kept in the working tree, deliberately not published.
# The public mirror is synced with robocopy /MIR, so without these it would keep
# re-adding them on every sync.
/ARCHITECTURE.md
/BUILD.md
/MIGRATIONS.md
/SECURITY.md
/TESTING.md

# Button set content — kept in the working tree, deliberately not published.
# Same reasoning as the internal documentation above, and the same trap: this
# file is itself synced by robocopy /MIR, so the rules have to live HERE, in the
# working tree. Adding them only to the mirror's copy lasts exactly until the
# next sync overwrites it.
#
# Both the built bundles and the specs are excluded, because the specs hold the
# same commands in source form — excluding one without the other would publish
# the content anyway.
/ButtonSets/
/tools/buttonset-gen/
/src/shared/shipped-button-sets.test.ts

# Website hand-off briefs — internal, like the documentation above. Kept at the
# repository root rather than in release/, because `npm run clean` deletes
# release/ wholesale and took the 1.3.0 brief with it once.
/WEBSITE-UPDATE-*.md
